      ],
      "source": "x:n1",
      "destination": "x:n2",
      "description": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n0-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "Systematic application of statistical methods to detect problematic data and testing hypotheses of its prevalence could be done within the ClinicalTrials.gov (CT) database"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n1-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "As a result, patients were exposed to increased risk instead of decreased risk"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n2-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "researchers are often quite bad in fabricating data that look genuinely stochastic"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n3-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "Whether problematic data is detected is therefore highly dependent on how the data is problematic"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n4-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "severely different baseline measures for two randomized groups"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n6-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "The proposed project lasts six months"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n7-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "The application of these methods to the ClinicalTrials.gov data is postponed until the statistical properties of these methods are further investigated"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:r2-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "Since these groups are expected to be statistically similar, if severe differences do occur"
    }
  ]
}